# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  TAG 1 · MORGEN · DIE FÄHRE — Prolog und Vordeck
#  Ablauf: 08:00 Start · 09:30 Inya sucht Rowan · 09:45 Schiff erkennt den Wildcard · 10:25 Horn · 10:40 Anlegen
#  Kanon: bible/places/ferry_*.json, bible/intro.txt
#
#  WISSENSMODELL (wer weiß am Morgen was über Rowan?)
#    · Öffentlich: am Brückendeck hängt die Passagierliste, 37 getippte Namen und einer in Tinte: "Vance, R. — Wildcard".
#      Jeder Erstsemester trägt seit dem Hafen eine Jacke (per Post gekommen); Rowan ist der Einzige ohne.
#    · Nathan hat die Liste gelesen, weiß aber nicht, WER es ist, bis Rowan seinen Nachnamen nennt (told_wildcard).
#    · Scharfe Beobachter (Gideon, Magnus, Teobalt) schließen es aus Liste plus fehlender Jacke.
#    · Alle anderen erfahren es von Rowan, von Nathan (der alles weitererzählt) oder um 09:45 (ship_knows_wildcard).
#  Rowan ist ein vollwertiger Gesprächspartner: gesprochene Optionen werden automatisch von ihm laut gesagt.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

@place ferry_deck
  known
  travel 0
  onArrive ferry_prologue
  object nathan sprite=nathan x=27 y=98 h=64 label="Nathan" scene=ferry_nathan when day=1 and time<10:40 and flag_prologue_done and not follow_nathan
  object baylee sprite=baylee x=14 y=99 h=78 label="Baylee" scene=ferry_baylee when day=1 and time<10:40 and flag_prologue_done and not follow_baylee
  object ed sprite=ed x=56 y=84 h=56 label="Boy in a hat" scene=ferry_ed when day=1 and time<10:40 and not met:ed
  object ed_m sprite=ed x=56 y=84 h=56 label="Ed" scene=ferry_ed when day=1 and time<10:40 and met:ed
  object georgie sprite=georgie x=76 y=100 h=46 label="Girl with the dark-blue feather" scene=ferry_georgie when day=1 and time<10:40 and not met:georgie
  object georgie_m sprite=georgie x=76 y=100 h=46 label="Georgie" scene=ferry_georgie when day=1 and time<10:40 and met:georgie
  object branden sprite=branden x=100 y=100 h=40 label="Flame-haired kid" scene=ferry_branden when day=1 and time<10:40 and not met:branden
  object branden_m sprite=branden x=100 y=100 h=40 label="Branden" scene=ferry_branden when day=1 and time<10:40 and met:branden
  object pippa sprite=pippa x=88 y=96 h=58 label="Girl with a camera" scene=ferry_pippa when day=1 and time<10:40 and not met:pippa
  object pippa_m sprite=pippa x=88 y=96 h=58 label="Pippa" scene=ferry_pippa when day=1 and time<10:40 and met:pippa
  object mikoto sprite=mikoto x=42 y=101 h=56 label="Boy with a gull" scene=ferry_mikoto when day=1 and time<10:40 and not met:mikoto
  object mikoto_m sprite=mikoto x=42 y=101 h=56 label="Mikoto" scene=ferry_mikoto when day=1 and time<10:40 and met:mikoto
  action rail "Lean on the bow rail" scene=deck_rail when day=1 and time<10:40
  action collars "Count the collars" scene=deck_collars when day=1 and time<10:40
  action lighthouse "Look for the lighthouse" scene=deck_lighthouse when day=1 and time<10:40 and time>=9:30
  action seasick "Be seasick" scene=deck_seasick when day=1 and time<10:40

@event ship_figures_it_out scene=ship_figures_it_out day=1 from=09:45 when not ship_knows_wildcard and (at:ferry_deck or at:ferry_lounge or at:ferry_stern or at:ferry_bridge)

# ───────────────────────────── PROLOG ─────────────────────────────

@scene ferry_prologue once bg=ferry_deck music=menu
  Salt on your lips. An engine thrumming somewhere under your shoes. You must have dozed off against the railing.
  You open your eyes to a morning so bright it hurts. The ferry left the mainland in the dark, and since then there has been nothing but water.
  Now there is an island.
  It is still far off: a grey volcano with a thin thread of smoke above it, jungle down its flanks, one white speck that must be a lighthouse. Caldera Key. Pixel Academy.
  Two weeks ago you were folding other people's sheets in Aunt Dee's laundromat, phone propped against the detergent shelf, climbing the online ladder one match at a time between dryer cycles.
  Best_Tarleinn. Top ten on the ladder for your age bracket. Winner of the Wildcard Qualifier — the last open seat of the year.
  You have never once played this game on a real table. Never shuffled a real deck in front of a real person who was looking at your hands.
  Your deck box sits in the pocket of your old rain jacket. Gather That Storm. Seventy-four cards, counting the three heroes and their six starting abilities, and you know every one of them by heart.
  The acceptance letter is still in your bag, folded so often it has gone soft. At the bottom, in smaller print: "Housing: The Commons, Bungalow 7 (late admission)."
  Folded inside the letter, a small canvas pouch: a hundred and forty Smug Coins, one starting purse for every student on the island, each stamped with a smirking little face. The Academy's own money. Good here, and nowhere else. The few folded notes in your sock, which are every scrap of mainland money you own, are worth exactly nothing past the arch.
  You do not know yet what that means.
  The deck around you is full: duffel bags, deck boxes, thirty-odd people your age in stiff new uniform jackets, red and gold and black. Every one of them is a stranger. They received their jackets in the post a month ago. Yours, the letter says, will be issued on arrival, which makes you the only one on deck in a rain jacket and the only one who looks like it.
  A loudspeaker crackles above the wheelhouse.
  [?Loudspeaker] "Morning, all. Captain Stroud speaking. Thirty-eight new heads aboard, I counted twice. We tie up at ten-forty. There is coffee in the lounge. Hold on to your hats."
  @enter nathan x=30 y=98 h=64
  [nathan?=laughing!] "**DUDE.** Is that it? That's *IT*, right? That's the island! Hey — **HEY**, big guy, look, that's the island!"
  The shout comes from about a foot behind your ear. Its owner has a square face, spiky charcoal hair standing up like a crown with one magenta clip at the temple, a chipped front tooth and the widest grin you have seen all week. He points at the volcano with his whole arm.
  @enter baylee x=14 y=99 h=78
  The "big guy" is not hard to find. He is the tallest person on the deck by a head and a half, in a straw hat as wide as a cartwheel, sunburnt, built like a barn door, his jacket slung over one shoulder, and he stands with his shoulders pulled in so that people can get past him.
  [baylee?=shy] "…I see it."
  [nathan?=happy] "Nathan Whisper! War Counselors, best deck in the format, don't let anyone tell you different. You look wrecked. You a first-year too? What dorm? I got something called the Commons, sounds fancy."
  @meet nathan
  @deckinfo nathan
  He sticks out a hand. Behind him the giant gives you a small nod.
  [baylee?] "Baylee. Commons too. …He has been like this since the harbour."
  @meet baylee
  @flag flag_prologue_done
  @learn ferry_lounge
  @learn ferry_stern
  @learn ferry_bridge
  Nathan's hand is still out. Two strangers are waiting to find out who you are, and nobody has told you yet how much of it you have to say.
  @choice How do you introduce yourself?
    > "Rowan Vance. Yes, first-year, and I think I'm in the Commons as well, bungalow seven. I only got my housing two weeks ago, so I'm still catching up on what any of this means."
      @aff nathan +2 | Introduced himself properly
      @aff baylee +1 | Polite hello
      @follow nathan baylee
      You take the hand. It shakes yours the way a pump handle would, if the pump were delighted.
      [nathan=happy] "SEVEN! That's — hold on. Hold on. Vance? Vance, R.?"
      He lets go of your hand and stares at you with the kind of expression normally reserved for a UFO.
      [nathan=laughing] "There's a name on the passenger list. By the wheelhouse door. In INK, like somebody added it with a fountain pen at the last minute. 'Vance, R. — Wildcard.' Nobody knows who it is! There's a whole betting pool going on the lounge benches about who it is! That's YOU?"
      ~ I never told him my last name was on a list. It's on a list.
      @flag nathan_read_list
      @choice
        > "Yes, that's me. I won the Wildcard Qualifier two weeks ago, the last open seat of the year. I still feel a bit strange saying it out loud."
          [nathan=happy] "THE LAST OPEN SEAT! Baylee, he got the last seat! That's like winning the lottery but with cards!"
          [baylee] "Congratulations."
          [nathan=grin] "That's — Rowan. Rowan! You're famous! You're the whole boat's mystery! I've got to tell everyone!"
          [rowan] "Please don't tell everyone. I only just got here."
          [nathan=laughing] "I'm already telling everyone!"
          @flag told_wildcard
          @flag ship_knows_wildcard
          @aff nathan +1 | Was honest about it
        > "Yes. But I would honestly rather the whole boat didn't hear about it before I've even found the lounge."
          [nathan=happy] "Oh. OH. You're shy! That's fine! I get it! I'll only tell, like, half the boat!"
          [baylee] "Nathan."
          [nathan=grin] "A quarter! A QUARTER of the boat."
          [baylee] "He will tell all of it."
          [nathan=laughing] "I will tell all of it."
          @flag told_wildcard
          @flag ship_knows_wildcard
          @aff nathan +1 | Asked him to keep quiet
          @aff baylee +1 | Asked for discretion
        > Admit it and ask him to tell nobody until you have had breakfast.
          [rowan] "That's me. I'd like to keep it quiet until I've had something to eat and found my feet. Could you do that for me?"
          Nathan puts a hand over his mouth, which lasts about four seconds.
          [nathan=happy] "I can do that! I can absolutely not do that! But I'll try! That's honest!"
          [baylee] "He means it."
          [baylee] "He'll still tell."
          @flag told_wildcard
          @aff nathan +2 | Trusted him with it
          @aff baylee +1 | Asked for discretion
    > "Rowan. Just Rowan for now. I'm in the Commons too, apparently. Have you had a look round the ship yet? Anything worth finding?"
      @follow nathan baylee
      [nathan=laughing] "ROWAN! Just Rowan! Like a wizard!"
      [baylee] "Like a bartender."
      [nathan=grin] "Like a WIZARD bartender. Okay. I like you. You asked ME a question. Nobody asked me a question since the harbour, they all just ran away!"
      @aff nathan +2 | Asked him something
      @aff baylee +1 | Polite hello
      @flag nathan_gave_tour
    > Shake his hand and say only that you are tired and new, and that you would rather listen for a while.
      @aff nathan +1 | Shook on it
      @aff baylee +1 | Polite hello
      @follow nathan baylee
      [rowan] "Tired, and new. I'm going to listen for a bit, if that's all right. I think I came here with too many questions."
      [nathan=happy] "A listener! Okay, okay, I can talk for TWO people. That's my second-best skill!"
      [baylee] "What's the first?"
      [nathan=grin] "Talking for three!"
  [nathan=laughing] "Okay, listen. Down those steps there's a lounge with an actual card table, green felt and everything. A guy in white gloves has sat at it all morning. Gideon something. Won three in a row."
  [nathan=grin] "And there's this tiny girl with green hair, Inya, she's been waiting twenty minutes to play him and he won't. He just sits there. And a kid called Tomi is taking bets on it. Bets! On a boat!"
  [nathan=happy] "Also, at the back there's a girl with three treasure chests. Real ones. I counted. And the captain lets you look at the steering wheel if you ask nice."
  Under the wheelhouse a door stands open on a flight of steps. You can hear it from here: cards slapping on felt, a girl's voice, quick and sharp, and a second voice that stays low and does not hurry. A few people on the benches have turned their heads that way.
  A side deck runs aft past the funnel to the stern, where gulls hang over the wake. An iron stair climbs to the wheelhouse door. The island stands dead ahead, still small. The clock over the lounge door says eight.
  @choice What do you do?
    > "Show me this card table. I want to see how he plays."
      @aff nathan +1 | Wanted to see the table
      [nathan=happy] "THAT'S what I'm talking about. Baylee, he's a table guy!"
      [baylee] "Seems so."
      @time 3
      @jump toward_lounge
    > "I'd like to have a look at the whole ship first. Come with me, if you want."
      [nathan=grin] "Tour! Yes! I'm basically a tour guide! Baylee, we're a tour!"
      [baylee] "We're a tour."
      @aff nathan +1 | Took him along
      @aff baylee +1 | Took him along
      @time 5
      @jump stay
    > Stay at the rail and watch the island come closer.
      Nathan's mouth opens, thinks better of it, and closes. It is perhaps the longest he has been silent since the harbour.
      [baylee] "Let him look, Nathan."
      [nathan] "I'll be around! I'm always around! I'm on the whole ship!"
      The two of them peel away along the rail. The island does not look any nearer, but it does look more real.
      @time 10
      @jump stay
  @label toward_lounge
  @goto ferry_lounge 2
  @scene lounge_first
  @end
  @label stay
  ~ Calm down. Nobody here has seen you play. Nobody even knows who Best_Tarleinn is.
  The deck is yours for the moment. The ship has several places in it, and a lot of people who have not yet decided what they think of you.
  @end

@scene ship_figures_it_out
  A cheer goes up near the lounge steps, a sharp ripple of laughter, and then a girl's voice, high and delighted, calling across the whole deck: "It's the one without the jacket! It's the jacket!"
  Heads turn. Thirty-odd people check the collar of every other person, then the single rain jacket, and arrive, one by one, at the same conclusion.
  The passenger list has been read, the arithmetic has been done, and the ship has worked out which of its passengers was added in ink.
  ~ Well. That didn't take long.
  @flag ship_knows_wildcard
  @time 0

# ───────────────────────────── DECK: ORTSHANDLUNGEN ─────────────────────────────

@scene deck_rail
  The bow rail is cold and wet and exactly the right height for elbows.
  @if time<9:00
    The island is still a smudge with ambitions. You can only tell it from the clouds by its edges.
  @elif time<10:00
    The island has grown a mountain. A real one: a grey cone with a thread of smoke and jungle running down its flanks to pale sand. A white speck at its foot has become a lighthouse.
  @else
    You can make out the shape of the bay now, the pier, a line of low roofs. A white building on the hill catches the sun like a dropped coin.
  ~ In two weeks I will be on a real table in front of real people. I will be fine. I will be fine.
  Somewhere behind you Nathan is telling somebody about the plate.
  @if not found_rail_coins
    Down by the foot of the rail, between two planks beside the lifebuoy, something small and gold winks at you. Two Smug Coins, wedged tight, that somebody lost their nerve over. You prise them out with a thumbnail.
    @coins 2
    @flag found_rail_coins
  @time 10

@scene deck_collars
  You lean against a bollard and count collars.
  Every first-year wears the same red jacket with one of three collars: white with a gold edge, blue, or plain grey. The white-and-gold ones stand a little apart from the others without seeming to try. The blue ones are scattered through the crowd. The grey ones hold their bags in both arms.
  You count seven white, twelve blue, eighteen grey. That makes thirty-seven, and the one without a collar at all is the thirty-eighth.
  It is not important until somebody tells you what the colours mean.
  @flag counted_collars
  @time 5

@scene deck_lighthouse
  You borrow the captain's trick of squinting at the horizon, and there it is: a white pencil stroke on the cliff south of the bay. The lighthouse.
  Beyond it, as the ferry swings its nose, you catch a second tower on the cliff and a thin white line of beach with a row of tiny roofs along it. The Commons, if the rumours are true. They look like a row of sugar cubes.
  @flag saw_commons_roofs
  @time 5

@scene deck_seasick
  You have not been seasick for the whole crossing. This seems a waste of an opportunity.
  You try it anyway, leaning over the leeward rail with a look of great suffering. A gull lands on the rail and stares at you with open scorn.
  ~ Not even the birds are fooled.
  @time 5

# ───────────────────────────── DECK: FIGUREN ─────────────────────────────

@scene ferry_nathan
  @if var:ferry_talked>=5
    [nathan=laughing] "You've talked to — what — SIX people already? I was going to say seven! Baylee, pay me!"
    [baylee] "I did not bet."
    [nathan=grin] "You will!"
  @elif var:ferry_talked>=2
    [nathan=grin] "Hey! I heard you talked to somebody! Everyone's talking about it! Okay, I started it, but still!"
    @choice
      > "What exactly did you tell them about me?"
        [nathan=happy] "Only true things! That you're polite, that you shook my hand, and that you have a rain jacket."
        [rowan] "That's — fair."
        [nathan=laughing] "No offence!"
        @aff nathan +1 | Asked him straight
      > "Please remember that I haven't told you much, so you can't have much to repeat."
        [nathan=grin] "I made up the rest! That's okay, right? Most of it was flattering."
        @aff nathan +0 | Joked with him
  @elif told_wildcard
    [nathan=happy] "Rowan! I've told eleven people you're the Wildcard. Is that okay? I told them before you said it was okay."
    @choice
      > "It's all right. Just let me say the next bit myself."
        [nathan=grin] "Deal! I'll hold the introductions! I'll only do the volume!"
        @aff nathan +2 | Fair deal
      > "Nathan, I asked you to keep it quiet."
        [nathan=laughing] "You did! And I did! For four seconds! That's a personal best!"
        @aff nathan -1 | Told everyone anyway
  @else
    [nathan=happy] "Rowan! I've told everybody about the list, the one with the ink name! Nobody knows who it is! There's a pool going!"
    @choice
      > "Nathan, I'm the one in ink. Vance, R. Please don't announce it yet."
        [nathan=happy] "THAT'S YOU. THAT'S —" He claps both hands over his own mouth. A pause. "…sorry. Sorry. Sorry. I'm not telling. Nobody. Not a soul. That's the best secret I've ever had and I'm going to hold it for at least ten minutes."
        @flag told_wildcard
        @aff nathan +2 | Trusted him with it
      > "I hope they find out soon." @hint Keep it to yourself
        [nathan=grin] "Right?! The suspense is killing me!"
  @aff nathan +1 | Heard him out
  @time 5
  @if not chat_nathan_offered
    @flag chat_nathan_offered
    @scene chat_nathan

@scene ferry_baylee
  @if not flag_baylee_chat
    Baylee stands with one hand on the rail, as if holding the ship in place while the rest of it moves.
    [baylee] "Morning."
    @choice
      > "Morning. Sorry about before, I think I ran over your introduction. Is he always like this?"
        [baylee] "Yup." A pause long enough to watch a gull cross the sky. "Met him at the harbour. Sat next to me on the bus. Told me about his whole family before the first stop."
        [baylee] "Ten minutes in, I figured he was either going to be a problem or the best thing that happened to me this year."
        [rowan] "Which was it?"
        [baylee] "Still working that out."
        He says it without a smile, but something in the sunburnt face loosens a little.
      > "I didn't catch much of that. Where are you from, Baylee?"
        [baylee] "North of everything. Farm. Dairy, mostly. Some corn." Another pause. "Cows are easier to talk to. They tell you when they're upset."
        ~ He said that completely seriously, and somehow it is the most reassuring thing anyone has said to me all week.
        @aff baylee +2 | Asked about home
        @flag baylee_from_farm
    @choice
      > "He seems all right, actually. Loud, but all right."
        [baylee] "He is." Quietly. "Loud. But he said hello to me first. Nobody does that."
        @aff baylee +2 | Agreed about Nathan
      > "Do you play? What do you run?"
        [baylee] "Big Stomp. Dinosaurs." He holds up a hand the size of a dinner plate, deck box lost in it. "Not good. Fun, though."
        @scene mutter_baylee
        [baylee] "You can have a game later. If you want. If you're not busy."
        @aff baylee +1 | Offered a game
        @flag baylee_game_offered
      > "I'm a bit nervous about today, to be honest. First real table, first real people."
        [baylee] "Yup." A very long pause. "Me too. Big boy, small ship. Everybody looks."
        [baylee] "Tables are just tables, though. They hold things up."
        @aff baylee +3 | Shared a worry
        @flag told_baylee_nerves
    @flag flag_baylee_chat
    @time 8
  @else
    Baylee is where he was, which seems to be the general policy.
    [baylee] "Yup?"
    @choice
      > "How is the crossing treating you?"
        [baylee] "Long. Good long. Haven't been on a boat since the county fair ferry, and that was two minutes."
        @aff baylee +1 | Small talk
      > "Mind if I stand here a while and ask you a few things?" @if not chat_baylee_done
        @scene chat_baylee
      > "Do you fancy that game now?" @if baylee_game_offered and not flag_baylee_game
        [baylee] "…Could do. Quick one. Casual."
        @scene deck_baylee
        @duel ferry_baylee deck=baylee name="Baylee Halvorsen"
          @win
            [baylee] "Good game. You've got — a way with the sky, with that deck. Looks like rain's coming in all at once."
            @aff baylee +2 | Good game
          @lose
            [baylee] "Huh." He looks at his big dinosaurs for a long moment. "Lucky. Sorry."
            @aff baylee +2 | Won kindly
        @scene post_baylee
        @flag flag_baylee_game
        @time 25
      > Leave him to his rail.
        [baylee] "Thanks."
    @time 5
  @if met:baylee and not chat_baylee_offered
    @flag chat_baylee_offered
    @scene chat_baylee

@scene ferry_ed
  @if not met:ed
    Somebody is hanging off the bow rail by one hand.
    He is hanging the way other people stand, entirely at ease, the other hand holding a battered cowboy hat in place against the wind. The sea slides past thirty feet below his dangling boots. Nobody else on the deck seems to find this remarkable.
    [ed?] "Hey! Hey, you! Can you see it? The volcano? It's got a CRATER. I read about it. There's a hole in the middle you can walk down into!"
    @choice
      > "I can see it. But would you mind coming back over the rail first? I'd rather not watch you go in."
        [ed?] "Is it — is it dangerous, coming back over? That's what I'd want to know."
      > "That's a very long drop. I'm Rowan, by the way. Does that hand ever get tired?"
        [ed?] "Rowan! Nope! It's the other hand that gets tired. I switch."
    He swings a leg up, hooks it over the rail with the grace of a boy who has done this on fences, and lands in a crouch on the planks, grinning like the sun just rose.
    [ed] "Ed Venture. Lazy V Ranch, up on the high plains. Bungalow five, supposedly. They put the Commons on a beach. A BEACH."
    @meet ed
    @add ferry_talked +1
    [ed] "What's yours?"
    @choice
      > "Rowan Vance. I'm in the Commons too, bungalow seven, so two doors down from you. I got in late, so I'm still finding out what's where."
        [ed] "Two doors down! Rowan! That's a good name, it goes up and down, like a horse on a hill."
        @aff ed +2 | Same dorm row
      > "Rowan. I'd rather you didn't fall in the sea. I've only just met you."
        [ed] "Aw, I won't. I've got — I always have a plan. It's a small plan, usually, but it's got steps."
        @aff ed +1 | Worried about him
      > "Rowan Vance. What's the most dangerous place on the island, do you think?" @hint Bold
        Ed's whole face lights up like a pinball machine.
        [ed] "Okay. Okay okay okay. I've got a MAP. Hang on. Not on me. It's in my bag. It's got all the forbidden places on it. Volcano rim, ruins field, the north shore — I'm going to go to all of them. All of them! You in?"
        [rowan] "I'll think about it."
        [ed] "That's a yes in ranch!"
        @aff ed +3 | Shared his enthusiasm
        @flag ed_map_offered
    @time 10
  @else
    @if not flag_ed_game
      Ed has his hat on and his sleeves rolled and a look of bright, unfocused enthusiasm.
      [ed] "Rowan! You want to play? On the rail? I'd do it on the rail, but they say that's against the rules, which is a real shame."
      @choice
        > "Sure, let's play. On a bench, with both feet on the ground."
          [ed] "Fine, fine! Both feet! Mostly!"
          @scene deck_ed
          @duel ferry_ed deck=ed name="Ed Venture"
            @win
              [ed] "Ha! Whoa! You did a thing with the lightning! I didn't see that thing coming. Is it — would you say it's dangerous? That deck?"
              @aff ed +2 | Loved the loss
            @lose
              [ed] "WHOOP! Grab the shiny thing and figure it out on the way down! Good game, Rowan! GOOD game!"
              @aff ed +2 | Won happily
          @scene post_ed
          @flag flag_ed_game
          @time 25
        > "Maybe later. I want to see the rest of the ship."
          [ed] "Later! Great! Later's my second favourite time!"
        > "First, tell me about the ranch." @if not chat_ed_done
          @scene chat_ed
    @else
      [ed] "Rowan! Hey! Did you see the lighthouse? It's real. They keep it lit even in the daytime! I asked the captain! Is that dangerous? Lighting it in the day?"
      @aff ed +1 | Chatted
      @time 5
  @if met:ed and not chat_ed_offered
    @flag chat_ed_offered
    @scene chat_ed

@scene ferry_georgie
  @if not met:georgie
    She is sitting on a coil of rope with a deck box held in both hands, in a jacket at least one size too big, its cuffs turned back twice. A dark-blue feather is pinned in her wild black hair. A girl with a camera is orbiting her with great concentration.
    [pippa?] "Chin up. No — down. No — up again. Look at the volcano like it owes you money."
    The girl on the rope looks at the volcano. It does not owe her money. Her face says so.
    She notices you looking and goes the colour of a tomato.
    [georgie?] "Sorry. Was I — is this your rope?"
    @choice
      > "No, it's not my rope. I'm Rowan, I was only looking at your deck box. Is it a good deck?"
        [georgie?] "Oh. Okay." She makes herself smaller, and then, quite suddenly, bigger. "It is. It's — yes. It's a very good deck. I'm Georgie. Sorry. Santa. Georgie Santa."
      > "Please sit wherever you like. I'm Rowan, by the way. Don't mind me."
        [georgie?] "Okay. Thank you. Georgie." She hesitates. "Santa. Georgie Santa. Sorry."
    @meet georgie
    @add ferry_talked +1
    @choice
      > "Is that a dragon on your bag?"
        A green plush dragon hangs from her backpack by one wing, much loved and slightly grey around the edges.
        [georgie] "Ember." Almost a whisper. "She's been to nationals twice. Please don't hold her by the wing."
        [rowan] "I won't. She looks like she's seen worse."
        [georgie] "She has." A tiny, startled smile. "…Thank you for asking first."
        @aff georgie +3 | Asked politely
        @flag georgie_ember
      > "Would you like to play a game, Georgie? Nothing riding on it, just for fun."
        [georgie] "…Yes." Almost inaudible. Then, braver: "Yes. Please. Not for anything. I don't — I'm not allowed to play for anything. But yes."
        @flag georgie_game_asked
        @aff georgie +2 | Asked for a game
        @jump georgie_game
      > "Nice to meet you, Georgie. I'll leave you in peace."
        [georgie] "Nice to — yes. You too. Sorry."
        @aff georgie +1 | Said hello
    @time 8
  @else
    @if flag_georgie_played
      Georgie is back to holding her deck box with both hands. The camera girl has moved on to somebody else's elbow.
      [georgie] "Hi, Rowan."
      @aff georgie +1 | Said hi
      @if not chat_georgie_done
        @choice
          > "May I ask you something? Only if you don't mind."
            @scene chat_georgie
          > Smile and let her be.
      @end
    @label georgie_game
    @if not flag_georgie_played
      You find a flat bit of deck. She opens her box with enormous care, as if the cards might wake.
      @choice
        > Play her.
          [georgie] "Thank you for the game."
          @scene deck_georgie
          @duel ferry_georgie deck=georgie name="Georgie Santa"
            @win
              Georgie stares at the board for a long time, completely still.
              [georgie] "…You didn't attack on turn three. I thought you'd attack on turn three." A pause. "I was really scared you'd notice that I had nothing."
              [rowan] "I noticed on turn four."
              [georgie] "That's — that's when it stopped working." A tiny wondering smile. "Good game. Really good game."
              @aff georgie +4 | Beat her fairly
              @flag beat_georgie
            @lose
              [georgie] "In response, I hatch." Quietly. Then, very small: "…That's your last Hero. Good game."
              [georgie] "Sorry."
              [rowan] "For what?"
              [georgie] "For winning. I always say it. I can't stop."
              @aff georgie +3 | Played well
          @scene post_georgie
          @flag flag_georgie_played
          @time 25
        > Tell her you would rather wait.
          [rowan] "Not right now. I'd love a game later, though, if that's all right."
          [georgie] "Okay. It's fine."
          @end
  @if met:georgie and not chat_georgie_offered and not flag_georgie_played
    @flag chat_georgie_offered
    @scene chat_georgie

@scene ferry_pippa
  @if not met:pippa
    A girl with a heavy old film camera hung round her neck is crouched on the deck, taking a picture of absolutely nothing.
    Strawberry-orange hair sticks up at the crown. There is a yellow bow tie under her chin and freckles on every visible surface.
    [pippa?] "Hang on — don't move — okay. Sorry. You were looking at the island with your hand on your jacket pocket. That's the shot. I got it."
    @choice
      > "I'm sorry, what shot? I'm Rowan, and I didn't know I was being photographed."
        [pippa?] "Light. Foreground. You were backlit. Good, actually." She lowers the camera. "Pippa Lund. I'm the photographer. Nobody asked me to be. I just got here first."
      > "Did you just take my picture? Do I get to see it, at least?"
        [pippa?] "Later! It's film. I'll develop it in a week. You'll hate it. It'll be perfect." She lowers the camera. "Pippa Lund. Photographer, by default."
    @meet pippa
    @add ferry_talked +1
    @choice
      > "Rowan Vance. I only came aboard in a hurry, so I'm not wearing the jacket they sent everybody else."
        @if ship_knows_wildcard
          [pippa] "Vance! The Wildcard. Your name's on the list at the wheelhouse door. In ink. Very dramatic."
          [rowan] "Is everyone going to say that?"
          [pippa] "Probably. Hope not. Might be sort of nice."
        @else
          [pippa] "Vance. Rowan Vance." She says it like a caption. "That'll be on the list at the wheelhouse door. I've been reading it. There's one name in ink and I think I've just found it."
          [rowan] "…You may have."
          [pippa] "I'm good at finding the thing in a picture that doesn't match."
          @flag told_wildcard
        @aff pippa +1 | Offered his name
      > "Is that an old film camera? I didn't think anybody still shot on film."
        [pippa] "Film is the only honest thing left." She turns it so you can see the dented brass. "You can't delete it. You get one frame, and you have to be sorry about it afterwards if it's bad."
        [pippa] "It was my aunt's. It has a light leak in the corner. I think it gives them character."
        @aff pippa +2 | Asked about her camera
        @flag pippa_film
      > "Do you always shoot strangers without asking?"
        [pippa] "Only the ones that hold still. Which — you did, actually. Quite well. Nobody's ever held that still for me."
        @aff pippa +1 | Held still
    @time 8
  @else
    [pippa] "Hang on — hang on —" She lifts the camera, clicks. "Sorry. Habit. How's the crossing?"
    @aff pippa +1 | Chatted
    @time 5
    @if not chat_pippa_done
      @choice
        > "Could I ask you something, while you're not shooting?"
          @scene chat_pippa
        > Nod and move on.
  @if met:pippa and found_lenscap and not lenscap_returned
    @choice
      > Give Pippa the lens cap you found.
        [pippa] "My — oh, my CAP! It was in the — I have been using a sock!" She presses it to her chest, then, quickly, onto the lens. "Click. Home. Where did you — never mind, don't tell me, I'll want it to be a mystery."
        [pippa] "You get a photograph. A good one. I'll have it by the end of the week."
        @item "Pippa's lens cap" -1
        @flag lenscap_returned
        @flag pippa_photo_promised
        @coins 5
        @aff pippa +4 | Returned her lens cap
      > Keep it a little longer.
  @if met:pippa and not chat_pippa_offered
    @flag chat_pippa_offered
    @scene chat_pippa

@scene ferry_mikoto
  @if not met:mikoto
    A thin boy in round glasses is addressing a gull.
    The gull has his sandwich. It sits on the rail, delicately lifting a corner of bread, while the boy holds out both hands as if to calm a small child.
    [mikoto?] "I'm sorry. I'm so sorry. It's just — that was my lunch. That was — I'm not angry. I just — sorry."
    The gull eats the sandwich.
    [mikoto?] "…Sorry."
    He notices you and laughs, a high, helpless giggle that stops as quickly as it started.
    [mikoto?] "Sorry! I'm Mikoto. I laugh when I'm frightened. It isn't funny. I know it isn't funny."
    @choice
      > "It's all right, really. I'm Rowan. And I think the gull won that one fair and square."
        [mikoto?] "She did. She really did." A breathless little laugh, and then, mercifully, a genuine smile.
      > "Don't apologise to the gull. I'm Rowan. Are you all right?"
        [mikoto?] "Oh — yes. No. A bit. I'm — thank you for asking, nobody asks."
    @meet mikoto
    @add ferry_talked +1
    @if ship_knows_wildcard
      [mikoto] "You're — oh. You're the one with the — Nathan told me everything. Wildcard. Rowan. Is it all right if I call you Row-Row? I won't. I'll ask first. May I?"
    @else
      [mikoto] "Rowan. That's a nice name. It sounds like a bird. Would it be all right — would you mind if I gave you a nickname? I won't. I'll ask first. May I?"
    @choice
      > "Sure. Row-Row is fine."
        [mikoto] "Row-Row!" A brilliant smile. "Oh, that's — thank you! I'll try not to — I'll use it sparingly!"
        @aff mikoto +3 | Allowed the nickname
        @flag mikoto_rowrow
      > "I'd rather keep it as Rowan, thanks. Maybe you can try again once we know each other better."
        [mikoto] "Rowan. Of course. Rowan." A tiny nod. "Sorry. I'll remember. I'll write it down."
        @aff mikoto +1 | Respectful
      > Offer to buy him a replacement sandwich.
        [rowan] "Let me get you another lunch. There's a galley hatch downstairs."
        [mikoto] "Oh — I couldn't — oh, would you?"
        You find him one at the lounge hatch later; it costs three Smug Coins and a lot of his gratitude.
        @coins -3
        @aff mikoto +4 | Bought him lunch
        @flag mikoto_sandwich
    @time 8
  @else
    @if not flag_mikoto_game
      [mikoto] "Rowan! Hi. Hello. Would you — would you like a game? You don't have to. I'll understand. I'm a bit — I'll apologise all the way through."
      @choice
        > "Sure, let's play. I'd like that."
          [mikoto] "Oh! Oh good. Oh no. I mean — good! I'll — sorry!"
          @scene deck_mikoto
          @duel ferry_mikoto deck=mikoto name="Mikoto Yamaguchi"
            @win
              [mikoto] "Sorry — sorry — you beat me — that's fine — that's what's supposed to happen — sorry — they get up again, you see. The skeletons. Nothing's ever properly finished."
              @aff mikoto +2 | Enjoyed the game
            @lose
              [mikoto] "I won? I'm sorry! I didn't — I'm — oh, I'm so sorry!" He laughs, stops, laughs again. "That was wonderful. Sorry."
              @aff mikoto +2 | Played with him
          @scene post_mikoto
          @flag flag_mikoto_game
          @time 25
        > "Maybe on the island, once I've got my bearings."
          [mikoto] "Of course. Of course. Sorry. On the island."
    @else
      [mikoto] "Rowan! Hello. The gull's still looking at me. I think she wants dessert."
      @aff mikoto +1 | Chatted
      @time 5
      @if not chat_mikoto_done
        @choice
          > "Do you mind if I ask you a few things? Only if it's all right."
            @scene chat_mikoto
          > Leave him to his gull.
  @if met:mikoto and not chat_mikoto_offered and not flag_mikoto_game
    @flag chat_mikoto_offered
    @scene chat_mikoto
